#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""api-credit: a persistent spend ledger for metered API-key sessions, and an
estimate of the prepaid credit left (provider-exact with an admin key).

Usage:
  api-credit hook                read a Stop/SessionEnd hook JSON on stdin and
                                 recompute that session's ledger entries from its
                                 transcripts; prints nothing, never fails the hook
  api-credit statusline [--json] read-only: one line (or, with --json, the balance
                                 object) for a statusline; nothing when
                                 SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER is unset
  api-credit balance [--json] [--month]
                                 live grants minus spend: provider-exact with an
                                 admin key (see Provider balance), else the
                                 ledger estimate; --month adds month-to-date
                                 spend (month_start, month_spend_usd,
                                 month_as_of, month_source, month_estimate,
                                 month_bridge_days)
  api-credit daily [--json]      per UTC day: sessions, spend, models (reconcile
                                 these rows against the provider console)
  api-credit calibrate AMOUNT [--at TIME]
                                 record AMOUNT (USD, read in the provider console)
                                 as the true balance at TIME (a full ISO-8601
                                 timestamp with offset or Z; default now): the
                                 balance becomes AMOUNT minus spend after it (see
                                 Anchor)

Everything is configured by environment variables; nothing is hardcoded.
  SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER  ledger path (JSONL). Unset or empty: hook and statusline
                     do nothing and exit 0; balance and daily exit 2.
  SYG_CREDIT_GRANTS  grants JSON path. Unset, missing or unparsable: the balance
                     is "spend only" (no remaining figure; one is never invented).
  SYG_CREDIT_ANCHOR  anchor file path (see Anchor). Unset or empty:
                     <SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER>.anchor.json.
  SYG_CREDIT_ROUTE   route label written into each entry (default anthropic-api).
  SYG_CREDIT_WHEN    NAME=value: the hook records only when the process env var
                     NAME equals value exactly (e.g. MY_ROUTE=metered; NAME= matches
                     a var that is set but empty; a value without "=" matches
                     nothing). Unset or empty: the metered route test below.
  SYG_CREDIT_FORCE=1 record regardless of the route rule (tests).
  SYG_CREDIT_PRICE_TABLE_CMD   replaces the sibling price-table program (a
                     command string, split like a shell would; --json is
                     appended). Tokens of the command that are existing files
                     are watched, so a change to one re-prices; a command
                     resolved via PATH (no slash) is not an existing file and
                     is not watched, so a change to it alone never re-prices.
                     For tests.
  SYG_CREDIT_NOW     ISO-8601 UTC "now" override (tests).
  ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_API_KEY  an organization Admin API key: turns on the provider
                     balance below for balance and statusline. Unset or empty:
                     no request is made and the output is the ledger estimate,
                     unchanged. Never printed, logged or passed in argv.
  SYG_CREDIT_ADMIN_KEY_CMD  a command string (split with shell quoting rules
                     (no ~ or $VAR expansion)): used only when
                     ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_API_KEY is empty; run only on a cache miss,
                     15 s timeout (SYG_CREDIT_KEY_CMD_TIMEOUT overrides for
                     tests), stdout stripped is the key, any failure is a
                     fetch failure cached for 60 s; it runs inside the caller,
                     so the statusline render waits for it on a cache miss:
                     point it at something fast (a cached read); the cache is
                     keyed by a hash of the command string, so a key rotated in
                     the store shows after at most the cache TTL.
  SYG_CREDIT_ADMIN_URL  replaces the Admin API origin (default
                     https://api.anthropic.com; tests point it at a loopback mock).
  SYG_CREDIT_SETTLE_DAYS  non-negative integer (default 2; unset, empty or
                     invalid means 2; 0 disables): the last N closed provider
                     days (as_of and the N-1 days before it, inside the fetch
                     window) take max(provider_day, ledger_day) until they
                     settle, and mark the balance an estimate while the ledger
                     figure is larger. A ledger that runs above the provider
                     counts the ledger figure for each such day (and marks the
                     balance "est") for as long as the day is in the window,
                     so a ledger that runs high keeps every close "est" for N
                     days; the price table is matched to the provider to keep
                     that rare.

Metered route test (with SYG_CREDIT_WHEN unset or empty): ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is
non-empty in the process environment AND ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL is empty or its host
is api.anthropic.com or ends in .anthropic.com. An empty ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (what
gateway presets set) is not metered.

Grants file (extra fields are ignored):
  {"currency":"USD","grants":[{"amount":200,"granted":"2026-10-08",
    "expires":"2026-10-21","tz":"UTC","kind":"promotional","note":"..."}]}
amount is a number > 0 (other grants are skipped); granted is required, expires
is optional. Each is a date YYYY-MM-DD, meaning 00:00 of that day in the grant's
tz (default UTC; an unknown tz skips the grant), or a full ISO-8601 timestamp
with offset or Z. A date-only expiry therefore lapses at the START of that day
(conservative).

Ledger: one JSON object per line, one per (session_id, day) where day is the UTC
date of each request's timestamp, so a session's spend is split by UTC day.
Fields: session_id, day, route, source ("transcript"), first_ts and last_ts (of
that day's requests), cost_usd, requests, request_ids (sorted), models
({model: {requests, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens,
cache_write_5m_tokens, cache_write_1h_tokens, web_search_requests,
web_fetch_requests, fast_requests, cost_usd}}), unpriced_models (sorted),
transcript_path, sources_sig (sorted [path, size, mtime_ns] of the transcript
files read and of the price source), updated_ts. The ledger file keeps its mode across rewrites (a new
one gets 0644 less the umask). Keys are sorted inside each line and lines are
sorted by (day, first_ts, session_id). Unparsable lines are preserved verbatim
on rewrite and ignored for the math. Entries written by older versions (no
source field) still count for balance and daily.

Spend accounting (the hook): the session's transcript_path plus every *.jsonl
under <its dir>/<session_id>/subagents/ is read. Each assistant line with a
message.usage object is one content block of a reply, and the reply's usage
repeats on each block with output_tokens growing, so per (message.id,
requestId) the line with the largest output_tokens is the request. Unparsable
lines are skipped (counted on stderr); <synthetic> models and requests with no
tokens are skipped. Token counts are exact per request. All of this runs under
the ledger lock. When every entry of the session carries a sources_sig equal to
the files' current one (os.stat only; a price-table change also triggers a
recompute), the call returns without reading transcripts or pricing. Otherwise
values are recomputed from the transcripts and replace that session's entries
wholesale, so re-running is idempotent; an unchanged result is not rewritten,
and a missing transcript_path is a no-op (recorded entries are never replaced
by nothing). A requestId already held by another session's entry (a resume or
fork copies earlier messages into the new transcript) is not counted again.

Pricing (cost is an estimate at the table's rates): `price-table --json` (same
bin dir) supplies USD per million tokens per model (exact id, else the id with a
trailing [...] suffix stripped, else with a trailing -YYYYMMDD date stripped,
after the bracket strip too). Cost = input*input + output*output +
cache_read*cacheRead + 5m writes*cacheWrite + 1h writes*(2*input). The 1h write
rate (2x input) is an assumption from the provider's published multipliers, not
a table field. A model's second rate card (price-table `long`: an `above`
threshold and four rates) prices the whole request when its prompt (input +
cache read + cache writes) is over the threshold. Not priced: the fast-mode premium (fast
requests are counted and priced at standard rates), server tool requests (web
search, web fetch: counted only), and models with no table row (tokens recorded,
no cost added, listed in unpriced_models). A failing price table aborts the call
(no write), so a transient failure cannot zero recorded spend.

Balance (an estimate): each ledger entry is a spend event at its last_ts. Events
are replayed in time order against the grants, drawing from the soonest-expiring
live grant first; a grant's unused remainder is forfeited when it expires. The
provider's real drawdown order is not documented; first-to-expire-first is an
assumption. Spend that no live grant covers is overage.
Each (session, UTC day) entry's spend is dated at its last_ts (and on the
provider path each cost_report bucket covers a whole UTC day, dated 23:59:59),
so a grant that is granted or expires mid-UTC-day (a non-UTC tz or a timestamp)
can see same-day spend replayed on the wrong side of its boundary; date-only
UTC grant times align with the day split and are exact.

Provider balance (balance and statusline only; hook and daily never fetch):
with ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_API_KEY or SYG_CREDIT_ADMIN_KEY_CMD set and a live grant,
the Admin API's /v1/organizations/cost_report is read (curl, 10 s timeout) from
00:00 UTC of the earliest live grant's granted day — moved back to the granted
day of any grant granted before it and expiring after it (or without expiry),
repeatedly, then clamped to at most 366 days before the start of the current
UTC day — up to the start of the current UTC day, so it covers closed UTC days
only (no closed day yet: no request). Each page is fetched with &limit=31 (the
Admin API's enforced max; the default is 7) and has_more/next_page pages are
followed (up to MAX_PAGES: at 31 buckets a page, a 366-day window fits; a page
size under the enforced max, a repeated token or exhausted pages are a failure
that falls back to the labeled estimate); a repeated next_page is a failure.
Only USD result rows count; each amount is a decimal string in cents. When the
window is unclamped, the provider's per-day sums inside it (with the last
SYG_CREDIT_SETTLE_DAYS closed days, default 2, taking max(provider_day,
ledger_day)) and the ledger's entries for every UTC day after the last provider
bucket (the whole window when the response has no dated bucket) are replayed
soonest-expiry first through the same drawdown as the ledger estimate; when
clamped, the replay starts with the ledger's entries from the earliest
overlapping grant's granted day up to the clamp day (so older grants' drawdown
before the clamp is the ledger's estimate, and ledger spend before every grant
is excluded). spent_usd is the provider's closed-day sums in the window
(settled with the ledger on the last N closed days) plus the bridged ledger
entries, plus, when clamped, the pre-window ledger entries since the earliest
overlapping grant. The object then carries source "provider", estimate (which
labels remaining_usd: false unless the window is clamped, a grant starts or
expires mid-UTC-day on a provider-bucket day, i.e. after the window start and
on or before provider_as_of, or a settle-window day used the ledger figure),
provider_as_of (the last bucket's UTC day, else the day before the window),
provider_window_start (the fetch window's start day, present whenever a fetch
was attempted), provider_chain_start (the earliest grant day of the overlap
chain), provider_clamped, provider_subday, provider_unsettled_days (the count
of settle-window days where the ledger figure won), ledger_lapsed_usd and
ledger_bridge_days (the number of distinct ledger days added). next_expiry and
days_left come from that replay; lapsed_usd is summed per grant, taking
in-window grants (granted at or after the earliest grant of the overlap chain)
from the provider replay and grants that lapsed before the chain from the
ledger replay (that ledger-sourced part is also reported as ledger_lapsed_usd).
The one-line text shows the bare figure (an estimate carries an "est" suffix)
and the balance command's second line names the basis and what the ledger
supplied ("provider through <day>; today[, lapses before <chain start>][, and
spend before <window start>], from the ledger", plus "; grant times mid-day"
when provider_subday is true). Any failure (curl error, timeout, HTTP >= 400,
non-JSON, no data array, an unparsable USD amount, a bucket with USD amounts
but no parsable starting_at, a repeated next_page, a non-finite sum) gives the
ledger estimate labeled source "ledger", estimate true, provider_as_of and
ledger_bridge_days null, and provider_window_start set to the window's start
day; it never fails the command. The fetch-attempt keys (source,
provider_as_of, provider_window_start, ledger_bridge_days) are present whenever
a fetch was attempted (anchored path included, with provider_unsettled_days on
the provider success path and provider_chain_start, provider_clamped,
provider_subday and ledger_lapsed_usd added on the unanchored provider success
path) and absent, with estimate true, when no fetch is attempted: no key (no
ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_API_KEY and no SYG_CREDIT_ADMIN_KEY_CMD, or an env key
containing CR or LF), no live grant, no closed day; a missing source means
ledger. The sum is cached at
${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/claude-statusline/api-credit-live.json (a JSON
object keyed by the key's SHA-256, the origin and the window, at most 4
entries; each value holds the sum, the as-of day and the per-UTC-day sums) and
reused for 300 s; a failure is cached the same way (as "failed") for 300 s (60 s
with "kind": "key-cmd" when SYG_CREDIT_ADMIN_KEY_CMD fails), so a broken
endpoint is not re-asked on every render; a corrupt or old-format cache, or one
without a valid per-day map, is refetched.

Anchor (calibrate): the ledger estimate is the grants minus ledger spend, blind
to card top-ups and to anything the ledger misprices. `calibrate AMOUNT` records
the balance read in the provider console as an anchor: it appends
{"amount", "at", "pre_anchor_day_usd", "recorded"} to the anchor file's
"anchors" list (history kept; rewritten atomically, mode kept) and prints the
anchor and the new balance line. pre_anchor_day_usd is the spend on the
anchor's UTC day before its instant, computed under the ledger lock: every
session in the ledger (entries of any day) whose transcript, the
transcript_path of its latest entry, was modified on or after 00:00 UTC of
that day is read once, and its requests of that day timed before the instant
count (those another session's entry holds excluded, the hook's rule, so a turn
no entry holds yet counts), priced like the hook; older transcripts cannot hold
that day's requests and are not read. That day's entries of the other sessions
(a transcript gone or older than the day) count whole when their last_ts is
before the instant, not at all when their first_ts is at or after it, and one
that straddles the instant refuses the calibrate (exit 1, nothing written).
AMOUNT is a finite number >= 0, --at a full timestamp no later than now (else
exit 2); an unparsable anchor file is never overwritten (exit 1). Known limit:
a session with no ledger entry at all at calibrate (its first turn not hooked
yet) is invisible; its spend before the instant later counts as spend after
it, so the balance reads low, never high.
The governing anchor is the readable record with the latest "at" no later than
now (an unparsable file or record is ignored for the balance; the balance
command says so on stderr for a file). With one, the balance is: (1) the grants
granted by the anchor are absorbed into AMOUNT: they are replayed to the
instant (ledger days before its day plus the pre-anchor spend) to learn each
one's remainder, and AMOUNT is allocated across them latest-expiring first (no
expiry counts as latest), each capped at its remainder and keeping its expiry,
the rest one cash pool without expiry; the drawdown assumption is
soonest-to-expire first, so money that survived to the instant sits in the
latest-expiring pools, and anything beyond the grants is a top-up; (2) grants
granted after the anchor enter unchanged; (3) the spend events are every
ledger entry after the anchor's day plus that day's ledger spend minus
pre_anchor_day_usd (clamped at 0), dated at the later of the instant and that
day's last request; (4) these are replayed as above, so spent_usd is the spend
since the anchor, and the object gains anchor_at and anchor_usd. (5) With the
admin key, the cost_report window runs from 00:00 UTC of the anchor's day to
the start of today; each closed day up to the as-of day takes the provider's
sum (the anchor's day minus pre_anchor_day_usd), later days the ledger's, and
the replay is redone with source "provider"; a failure labels the ledger
figure as above. The label stays "est" until a provider fetch covers the
post-anchor days.
"""
import argparse
import fcntl
import glob
import hashlib
import json
import math
import os
import re
import shlex
import signal
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from datetime import date, datetime, timedelta, timezone
from decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation
from urllib.parse import quote, urlparse

try:
    from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo
except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover
    ZoneInfo = None

DEFAULT_ROUTE = "anthropic-api"
MODEL_FIELDS = ("requests", "input_tokens", "output_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens",
                "cache_write_5m_tokens", "cache_write_1h_tokens", "web_search_requests",
                "web_fetch_requests", "fast_requests")
TOKEN_FIELDS = ("input_tokens", "output_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens",
                "cache_write_5m_tokens", "cache_write_1h_tokens")
EPS = 1e-9


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- time helpers

def utcnow():
    raw = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_NOW", "").strip()
    if raw:
        return parse_ts(raw)
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc)


def parse_ts(s):
    s = s.strip()
    if s.endswith("Z") or s.endswith("z"):
        s = s[:-1] + "+00:00"
    dt = datetime.fromisoformat(s)
    if dt.tzinfo is None:
        dt = dt.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)
    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc)


def iso(dt):
    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def money(x):
    return "{:.2f}".format(x)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- route test

def host_of(url):
    url = url.strip()
    if "://" not in url:
        url = "//" + url
    try:
        return (urlparse(url).hostname or "").lower()
    except ValueError:
        return ""


def is_metered():
    if os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_FORCE") == "1":
        return True
    if not os.environ.get("ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"):
        return False
    base = os.environ.get("ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL", "").strip()
    if not base:
        return True
    host = host_of(base)
    return host == "api.anthropic.com" or host.endswith(".anthropic.com")


def route_matches():
    """SYG_CREDIT_FORCE=1, else SYG_CREDIT_WHEN (NAME=value, exact match of a
    set var; no "=" matches nothing), else the metered route test."""
    if os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_FORCE") == "1":
        return True
    spec = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_WHEN", "")
    if spec:
        if "=" not in spec:
            return False
        name, value = spec.split("=", 1)
        return bool(name) and os.environ.get(name) == value
    return is_metered()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ledger io

def is_num(x):
    return isinstance(x, (int, float)) and not isinstance(x, bool) and math.isfinite(x)


def valid_entry(e):
    return (
        isinstance(e, dict)
        and isinstance(e.get("session_id"), str)
        and isinstance(e.get("day"), str)
        and isinstance(e.get("last_ts"), str)
        and is_num(e.get("cost_usd"))
    )


def read_ledger(path):
    """Return (entries, garbage_lines). Missing file: empty."""
    entries, garbage = [], []
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="surrogateescape") as f:
            for line in f:
                line = line.rstrip("\n")
                if not line.strip():
                    continue
                try:
                    e = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError:
                    garbage.append(line)
                    continue
                if valid_entry(e):
                    entries.append(e)
                else:
                    garbage.append(line)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    return entries, garbage


def write_ledger(path, entries, garbage):
    entries = sorted(entries, key=lambda e: (e["day"], e.get("first_ts", ""), e["session_id"]))
    lines = [json.dumps(e, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) for e in entries] + garbage
    write_atomic(path, lines)


def write_atomic(path, lines):
    """Replace path with lines (each newline-terminated) via a temp file in the
    same dir and os.replace."""
    d = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path))
    # Keep an existing file's mode (mkstemp creates 0600); a new one gets 0644 & ~umask.
    try:
        mode = stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(path).st_mode)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        umask = os.umask(0)
        os.umask(umask)
        mode = 0o644 & ~umask
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".api-credit.", suffix=".tmp", dir=d)
    try:
        os.fchmod(fd, mode)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8", errors="surrogateescape") as f:
            for ln in lines:
                f.write(ln + "\n")
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- transcripts

def transcript_sources(sid, tpath):
    """The session transcript plus its subagent transcripts (missing ones are
    skipped by the reader)."""
    sub = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(tpath), sid, "subagents")
    return [tpath] + sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(sub), "**", "*.jsonl"), recursive=True))


def count(x):
    return int(x) if is_num(x) and x > 0 else 0


def request_of(e):
    """One transcript line -> a request dict, or None when it is not a usage line."""
    if not isinstance(e, dict) or e.get("type") != "assistant":
        return None
    msg = e.get("message")
    if not isinstance(msg, dict) or not isinstance(msg.get("usage"), dict):
        return None
    u = msg["usage"]
    cc = u.get("cache_creation")
    if isinstance(cc, dict):
        w5m = count(cc.get("ephemeral_5m_input_tokens"))
        w1h = count(cc.get("ephemeral_1h_input_tokens"))
    else:
        w5m, w1h = count(u.get("cache_creation_input_tokens")), 0
    stu = u.get("server_tool_use")
    stu = stu if isinstance(stu, dict) else {}
    model = msg.get("model")
    rid = e.get("requestId")
    return {
        "model": model if isinstance(model, str) and model else "?",
        "message_id": msg.get("id") if isinstance(msg.get("id"), str) else None,
        "request_id": rid if isinstance(rid, str) and rid else None,
        "timestamp": e.get("timestamp"),
        "input_tokens": count(u.get("input_tokens")),
        "output_tokens": count(u.get("output_tokens")),
        "cache_read_input_tokens": count(u.get("cache_read_input_tokens")),
        "cache_write_5m_tokens": w5m,
        "cache_write_1h_tokens": w1h,
        "web_search_requests": count(stu.get("web_search_requests")),
        "web_fetch_requests": count(stu.get("web_fetch_requests")),
        "fast": u.get("speed") == "fast",
    }


def extract(paths):
    """(requests, skipped_lines). A reply's usage repeats on each content-block
    line with output_tokens growing: per (message.id, requestId) keep the line
    with the largest output_tokens (the rule usage-sweep uses)."""
    replies, skipped, anon = {}, 0, 0
    for p in paths:
        try:
            fh = open(p, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
        except FileNotFoundError:
            continue
        with fh:
            for raw in fh:
                if '"usage"' not in raw:
                    continue
                try:
                    e = json.loads(raw)
                except ValueError:
                    skipped += 1
                    continue
                r = request_of(e)
                if r is None:
                    continue
                if r["message_id"] is None:
                    anon += 1
                    key = ("line", anon)
                else:
                    key = (r["message_id"], r["request_id"])
                prev = replies.get(key)
                if prev is None or r["output_tokens"] > prev["output_tokens"]:
                    replies[key] = r
    out = []
    for r in replies.values():
        if r["model"] == "<synthetic>" or not any(r[k] for k in TOKEN_FIELDS):
            continue
        try:
            r["ts"] = parse_ts(r["timestamp"])
        except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError):
            continue  # no day to attribute it to
        out.append(r)
    return out, skipped


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pricing

def price_command():
    """The price-table argv without --json: SYG_CREDIT_PRICE_TABLE_CMD split when
    set, else the sibling price-table program."""
    override = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_PRICE_TABLE_CMD", "")
    if override:
        return shlex.split(override)
    return [sys.executable, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "price-table")]


def price_source_paths():
    """The files whose change means new prices: every token of the override
    command that is an existing file (so `python3 /x/pt` and `env X=1 /x/pt` both
    watch the script), else the sibling price-table file."""
    cmd = price_command()
    if os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_PRICE_TABLE_CMD", ""):
        return [t for t in cmd if os.path.isfile(t)]
    return [cmd[1]]


RATE_FIELDS = ("input", "output", "cacheRead", "cacheWrite")


def parse_long_card(card):
    if not isinstance(card, dict):
        return None
    above = card.get("above")
    if not is_num(above) or above <= 0 or above != int(above):
        return None
    if not all(is_num(card.get(k)) for k in RATE_FIELDS):
        return None
    out = {"above": int(above)}
    for k in RATE_FIELDS:
        out[k] = float(card[k])
    return out


def load_prices():
    """{model: rates} from the sibling price-table --json. Raises on failure."""
    cmd = price_command()
    res = subprocess.run(cmd + ["--json"], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True,
                         text=True, timeout=30, check=True)
    doc = json.loads(res.stdout)
    table = doc.get("table") if isinstance(doc, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(table, dict):
        raise ValueError("price-table --json has no table object")
    out = {k: dict(v) if isinstance(v, dict) else v for k, v in table.items()}
    long_cards = doc.get("long")
    if isinstance(long_cards, dict):
        for model, card in long_cards.items():
            if isinstance(out.get(model), dict):
                parsed = parse_long_card(card)
                if parsed is not None:
                    out[model]["long"] = parsed
    return out


def rates_for(prices, model):
    """Rates for a model id: the exact id, else with a trailing [...] suffix
    stripped, else with a trailing -YYYYMMDD date stripped (after the bracket
    strip too)."""
    base = re.sub(r"\[[^\]]*\]$", "", model)
    row = None
    for cand in (model, base, re.sub(r"-\d{8}$", "", model), re.sub(r"-\d{8}$", "", base)):
        row = prices.get(cand)
        if row is not None:
            break
    if not isinstance(row, dict):
        return None
    try:
        out = {k: float(row[k]) for k in RATE_FIELDS}
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return None
    long_card = parse_long_card(row.get("long"))
    if long_card is not None:
        out["long"] = long_card
    return out


def request_cost(r, rates):
    """USD, an estimate. 1h cache writes at 2x the input rate (an assumption from
    the provider's published multipliers; the table carries the 5m rate only);
    per-request threshold cards from the table are applied. Not priced: server
    tool requests and the fast-mode premium (standard rates are used)."""
    long_card = rates.get("long")
    if isinstance(long_card, dict):
        prompt = (r["input_tokens"] + r["cache_read_input_tokens"]
                  + r["cache_write_5m_tokens"] + r["cache_write_1h_tokens"])
        if prompt > long_card["above"]:
            rates = long_card
    return (r["input_tokens"] * rates["input"] + r["output_tokens"] * rates["output"]
            + r["cache_read_input_tokens"] * rates["cacheRead"]
            + r["cache_write_5m_tokens"] * rates["cacheWrite"]
            + r["cache_write_1h_tokens"] * 2 * rates["input"]) / 1e6


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hook

def sources_sig(paths, price_paths=()):
    """Sorted [path, size, mtime_ns] of the transcript files and the price source
    files that exist (os.stat only), stored in each entry so an unchanged session
    is not re-read; the price source is included so a table change re-prices."""
    out = []
    for p in list(paths) + list(price_paths):
        try:
            st = os.stat(p)
        except OSError:
            continue
        out.append([p, st.st_size, st.st_mtime_ns])
    return sorted(out)


def build_entries(sid, requests, prices, tpath, now, sig):
    """The ledger entries for one session: one per UTC day of its requests."""
    route = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_ROUTE", "") or DEFAULT_ROUTE
    days = {}
    for r in requests:
        days.setdefault(r["ts"].strftime("%Y-%m-%d"), []).append(r)
    out = []
    for day, rs in sorted(days.items()):
        models, total = {}, 0.0
        for r in rs:
            rates = rates_for(prices, r["model"])
            m = models.get(r["model"])
            if m is None:
                # An unpriced model's cost_usd is null: unknown, not zero.
                m = models[r["model"]] = dict(dict.fromkeys(MODEL_FIELDS, 0),
                                              cost_usd=None if rates is None else 0.0)
            m["requests"] += 1
            for k in TOKEN_FIELDS + ("web_search_requests", "web_fetch_requests"):
                m[k] += r[k]
            m["fast_requests"] += 1 if r["fast"] else 0
            if rates is not None:
                c = request_cost(r, rates)
                m["cost_usd"] += c
                total += c
        for m in models.values():
            if m["cost_usd"] is not None:
                m["cost_usd"] = round(m["cost_usd"], 10)
        unpriced = [name for name, m in models.items() if m["cost_usd"] is None]
        out.append({
            "session_id": sid, "day": day, "route": route, "source": "transcript",
            "first_ts": iso(min(r["ts"] for r in rs)), "last_ts": iso(max(r["ts"] for r in rs)),
            "cost_usd": round(total, 10), "requests": len(rs),
            "request_ids": sorted({r["request_id"] for r in rs if r["request_id"]}),
            "models": models, "unpriced_models": sorted(unpriced),
            "transcript_path": tpath, "sources_sig": sig, "updated_ts": iso(now),
        })
    return out


def comparable(entries):
    """Entries as canonical JSON, updated_ts dropped, for the no-rewrite check."""
    return sorted(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in e.items() if k != "updated_ts"}, sort_keys=True)
                  for e in entries)


def hook(payload):
    """Recompute one session's entries from its transcripts and upsert them."""
    ledger = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER", "")
    if not ledger or not route_matches() or not isinstance(payload, dict):
        return
    sid, tpath = payload.get("session_id"), payload.get("transcript_path")
    if not isinstance(sid, str) or not sid or not isinstance(tpath, str) or not tpath:
        return
    if not os.path.isfile(tpath):
        # No transcript (moved, cleaned up, or never kept): computing from nothing
        # would replace this session's recorded entries with none.
        return
    d = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(ledger))
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    # Everything from here runs under the lock, transcripts read included, so an
    # older snapshot can never overwrite a newer one.
    with open(ledger + ".lock", "a") as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        entries, garbage = read_ledger(ledger)
        paths = transcript_sources(sid, tpath)
        sig = sources_sig(paths, price_source_paths())
        old = [e for e in entries if e["session_id"] == sid]
        if old and all(e.get("sources_sig") == sig for e in old):
            return  # no transcript changed since these entries were computed
        requests, skipped = extract(paths)
        if skipped:
            print("api-credit: skipped %d unparsable transcript line(s)" % skipped, file=sys.stderr)
        prices = load_prices()
        now = utcnow()
        taken = set()
        for e in entries:
            if e["session_id"] != sid and isinstance(e.get("request_ids"), list):
                taken.update(x for x in e["request_ids"] if isinstance(x, str))
        mine = [r for r in requests if r["request_id"] is None or r["request_id"] not in taken]
        new = build_entries(sid, mine, prices, tpath, now, sig)
        if comparable(old) == comparable(new):
            return
        write_ledger(ledger, [e for e in entries if e["session_id"] != sid] + new, garbage)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- grants and balance

def parse_when(val, tz):
    if not isinstance(val, str) or not val.strip():
        raise ValueError("bad time")
    val = val.strip()
    if len(val) == 10:
        d = date.fromisoformat(val)
        return datetime(d.year, d.month, d.day, tzinfo=tz).astimezone(timezone.utc)
    s = val[:-1] + "+00:00" if val[-1] in "Zz" else val
    dt = datetime.fromisoformat(s)
    if dt.tzinfo is None:
        dt = dt.replace(tzinfo=tz)
    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc)


def load_grants():
    """(currency, [grant dicts]) or None when there is no usable grants config."""
    path = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_GRANTS", "")
    if not path:
        return None
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            cfg = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if not isinstance(cfg, dict) or not isinstance(cfg.get("grants"), list):
        return None
    out = []
    for g in cfg["grants"]:
        if not isinstance(g, dict) or not is_num(g.get("amount")) or g["amount"] <= 0:
            continue
        try:
            tzname = g.get("tz") or "UTC"
            tz = timezone.utc if tzname == "UTC" else ZoneInfo(tzname)
            granted = parse_when(g.get("granted"), tz)
            expires = parse_when(g["expires"], tz) if g.get("expires") else None
        except Exception:  # unknown tz, bad date, missing granted: skip this grant
            continue
        out.append({"amount": float(g["amount"]), "granted": granted, "expires": expires,
                    "remaining": float(g["amount"]), "lapsed": False})
    currency = cfg.get("currency") if isinstance(cfg.get("currency"), str) else "USD"
    return currency, out


FAR = datetime.max.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)


def live_of(grants, now):
    """The grants live at now: granted by then and not lapsed by balance()'s replay."""
    return [g for g in grants if not g["lapsed"] and g["granted"] <= now]


def balance(entries, grants_cfg, now):
    spent = sum(e["cost_usd"] for e in entries)
    result = {"estimate": True, "currency": "USD", "spent_usd": round(spent, 6),
              "remaining_usd": None, "overage_usd": 0.0, "lapsed_usd": 0.0,
              "live_grants": 0, "next_expiry": None, "days_left": None,
              "granted_total_live": 0.0}
    if grants_cfg is None:
        return result
    currency, grants = grants_cfg
    grants.sort(key=lambda g: (g["expires"] or FAR, g["granted"]))
    events = []
    for e in entries:
        try:
            events.append((parse_ts(e["last_ts"]), e["cost_usd"]))
        except ValueError:
            continue
    events.sort(key=lambda ev: ev[0])
    overage = lapsed = 0.0

    def lapse_upto(t):
        nonlocal lapsed
        for g in grants:
            if not g["lapsed"] and g["expires"] is not None and g["expires"] <= t:
                lapsed += g["remaining"]
                g["lapsed_usd"] = g["remaining"]
                g["remaining"] = 0.0
                g["lapsed"] = True

    for t, amount in events:
        lapse_upto(t)
        left = amount
        for g in grants:
            if left <= 0:
                break
            if g["lapsed"] or g["granted"] > t or g["remaining"] <= 0:
                continue
            take = min(left, g["remaining"])
            g["remaining"] -= take
            left -= take
        if left > EPS:
            overage += left
    lapse_upto(now)
    live = live_of(grants, now)
    remaining = sum(g["remaining"] for g in live)
    exps = [g["expires"] for g in live if g["remaining"] > EPS and g["expires"] is not None]
    nxt = min(exps) if exps else None
    result.update({
        "currency": currency,
        "remaining_usd": round(remaining, 6),
        "overage_usd": round(overage, 6),
        "lapsed_usd": round(lapsed, 6),
        "live_grants": len(live),
        "granted_total_live": round(sum(g["amount"] for g in live), 6),
        "next_expiry": iso(nxt) if nxt else None,
        "days_left": max(0, int((nxt - now) // timedelta(days=1))) if nxt else None,
    })
    return result


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- provider balance

ADMIN_URL = "https://api.anthropic.com"
LIVE_TTL = 300   # seconds a cached cost_report sum is reused (the statusline's render cadence)
KEY_CMD_FAIL_TTL = 60   # seconds a failed key command is cached before retrying
MAX_PAGES = 14   # ceil(366 daily buckets / 31 per page) + margin; page size live-verified


def day_start(dt):
    return dt.replace(hour=0, minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)


def admin_origin():
    return (os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_ADMIN_URL", "") or ADMIN_URL).rstrip("/")


def parse_cost_page(doc):
    """(USD spend as Decimal, last bucket day or None, has_more, next_page,
    {bucket day: USD Decimal}) for one cost_report page. Raises ValueError on a
    shape that cannot be summed."""
    data = doc.get("data") if isinstance(doc, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(data, list):
        raise ValueError("cost_report has no data array")
    total, last, bad, days = Decimal(0), None, 0, {}
    for item in data:
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            continue
        day = None
        try:
            day = parse_ts(item.get("starting_at")).strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
            last = day if last is None or day > last else last
        except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError):
            pass
        if day is not None:
            days.setdefault(day, Decimal(0))
        results = item.get("results")
        if not isinstance(results, list):
            continue
        for r in results:
            if not isinstance(r, dict) or r.get("currency") != "USD":
                continue
            amount = r.get("amount")
            try:
                if isinstance(amount, bool) or not isinstance(amount, (str, int, float)):
                    raise InvalidOperation
                cents = Decimal(str(amount))
                if not cents.is_finite():
                    raise InvalidOperation
            except InvalidOperation:
                bad += 1
                continue
            if day is None:
                # Spend without a day could not be placed in the per-day sums: the
                # whole page is unusable rather than a total the days disagree with.
                raise ValueError("a bucket with USD amounts has no parsable starting_at")
            total += cents / 100   # amounts are decimal strings in cents
            days[day] += cents / 100
    if bad:
        # An unknown amount makes the sum unknown: fall back rather than undercount.
        raise ValueError("%d unparsable USD amount(s)" % bad)
    nxt = doc.get("next_page")
    more = doc.get("has_more") is True and isinstance(nxt, str) and bool(nxt)
    return total, last, more, nxt, days


def fetch_cost_report(key, start, end):
    """{"spent": Decimal, "as_of": day, "days": {day: Decimal}} summed over the
    closed-day cost_report buckets in [start, end), or None on any failure. as_of
    is the last bucket's day, else the day before start (the whole window is then
    ledger-bridged); days holds each bucket's USD sum by its starting day. The
    key reaches curl on stdin (a -K config), never in argv; -q keeps ~/.curlrc out."""
    base = "%s/v1/organizations/cost_report?starting_at=%s&ending_at=%s&group_by[]=description&limit=31" % (
        admin_origin(), quote(iso(start), safe=":"), quote(iso(end), safe=":"))
    cfg = 'header = "x-api-key: %s"\n' % key.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace('"', '\\"')
    total, as_of, page, seen, days = Decimal(0), None, None, set(), {}
    for _ in range(MAX_PAGES):
        url = base + ("&page=%s" % quote(page, safe="") if page else "")
        try:
            res = subprocess.run(["curl", "-q", "-sfg", "-m", "10", "-K", "-",
                                  "-H", "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01", url],
                                 input=cfg, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=15)
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            return None
        if res.returncode != 0:
            return None   # transport failure, timeout or HTTP >= 400 (-f)
        try:
            spent, last, more, page, page_days = parse_cost_page(json.loads(res.stdout))
        except ValueError:
            return None
        total += spent
        for day, amount in page_days.items():
            days[day] = days.get(day, Decimal(0)) + amount
        if last is not None and (as_of is None or last > as_of):
            as_of = last
        if not more:
            return {"spent": total, "as_of": as_of or (start - timedelta(days=1)).strftime("%Y-%m-%d"),
                    "days": days}
        if page in seen:
            return None   # a repeated next_page makes no progress: a failure, not a loop
        seen.add(page)
    return None   # more pages than MAX_PAGES: treat as a failure, not a partial sum


def live_cache_path():
    root = os.environ.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME", "") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".cache")
    return os.path.join(root, "claude-statusline", "api-credit-live.json")


def admin_key_source():
    """("env", key) or ("cmd", cmd_string), or None when no key source is configured
    (or the env key contains CR or LF: a CR/LF key could inject a curl -K directive)."""
    key = os.environ.get("ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_API_KEY", "")
    if key:
        return None if "\r" in key or "\n" in key else ("env", key)
    cmd = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_ADMIN_KEY_CMD", "")
    return ("cmd", cmd) if cmd else None


def key_cmd_timeout():
    try:
        t = float(os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_KEY_CMD_TIMEOUT", ""))
        if math.isfinite(t) and t > 0:
            return t
    except ValueError:
        pass
    return 15


def resolve_admin_key(src):
    """The admin key string from src, running the command on demand for ("cmd", ...),
    or None when the command fails or prints an empty or multi-line value."""
    kind, val = src
    if kind == "env":
        return val
    try:
        argv = shlex.split(val)
        if not argv:
            return None
        proc = subprocess.Popen(argv, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True)
        try:
            out, _ = proc.communicate(timeout=key_cmd_timeout())
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            try:
                os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
            except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
                pass
            try:
                proc.communicate(timeout=2)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                pass
            return None
        key = out.decode("utf-8").strip()
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    if proc.returncode != 0 or not key or "\r" in key or "\n" in key:
        return None
    return key


MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES = 4   # cached cost_report windows kept in live_cache_path()
DEFAULT_SETTLE_DAYS = 2


def settle_days():
    """SYG_CREDIT_SETTLE_DAYS as a non-negative int; unset, empty or invalid -> 2."""
    try:
        n = int(os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_SETTLE_DAYS", "").strip())
        if n >= 0:
            return n
    except ValueError:
        pass
    return DEFAULT_SETTLE_DAYS


def settled_days(got, entries, start, end):
    """For each closed day in [start, end) up to got["as_of"], (d, dk, amount)
    where the last SYG_CREDIT_SETTLE_DAYS closed days (as_of and the N-1 days
    before it, limited to [start, end)) take max(provider_day, ledger_day) and
    older days take provider_day, plus the count of those days where the ledger
    figure won (ledger > provider + EPS) and the total excess added."""
    as_of = got["as_of"]
    days, d = [], start
    while d < end and d.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") <= as_of:
        days.append(d)
        d += timedelta(days=1)
    n = settle_days()
    as_of_date = date.fromisoformat(as_of)
    recent = {x.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") for x in days if 0 <= (as_of_date - x.date()).days < n}
    ledger_by_day = {}
    if recent:
        for e in entries:
            if e["day"] in recent:
                ledger_by_day[e["day"]] = ledger_by_day.get(e["day"], 0.0) + e["cost_usd"]
    out, unsettled, excess = [], 0, 0.0
    for d in days:
        dk = d.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
        prov = float(got["days"].get(dk, 0))
        amount = prov
        if dk in recent:
            led = ledger_by_day.get(dk, 0.0)
            if led > prov + EPS:
                amount = led
                unsettled += 1
                excess += led - prov
        out.append((d, dk, amount))
    return out, unsettled, excess


def provider_spend(src, start, end, now):
    """The closed-day provider spend, from the TTL cache (a JSON object keyed by
    the key's or command's SHA-256, the admin origin and the window, at most
    MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES entries) when it is under LIVE_TTL old, else fetched
    (resolving a command key on demand) and cached. None on any fetch or
    key-command failure, cached as {"failed": true} for LIVE_TTL (or
    KEY_CMD_FAIL_TTL with "kind": "key-cmd" when the key command failed); cache
    errors are ignored (a corrupt or old-format cache is refetched, never
    trusted)."""
    path = live_cache_path()
    raw_id = src[1] if src[0] == "env" else "cmd\0" + src[1]
    ident = "%s %s %s %s" % (hashlib.sha256(raw_id.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest(), admin_origin(),
                             iso(start), iso(end))
    cache = {}
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            raw = json.load(f)
        if isinstance(raw, dict):
            cache = {k: v for k, v in raw.items()
                     if isinstance(k, str) and isinstance(v, dict) and isinstance(v.get("fetched_at"), str)}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
    c = cache.get(ident)
    if isinstance(c, dict):
        try:
            age = (now - parse_ts(c["fetched_at"])).total_seconds()
            if c.get("failed") is True:
                ttl = KEY_CMD_FAIL_TTL if c.get("kind") == "key-cmd" else LIVE_TTL
                if 0 <= age < ttl:
                    return None
            elif 0 <= age < LIVE_TTL and isinstance(c["as_of"], str) and isinstance(c["spent"], str):
                spent = Decimal(c["spent"])
                # A record without a valid per-day map (an older shape) is a miss.
                raw_days = c.get("days")
                if not isinstance(raw_days, dict) or not all(
                        isinstance(k, str) and isinstance(v, str) for k, v in raw_days.items()):
                    raise ValueError("no per-day map")
                days = {k: Decimal(v) for k, v in raw_days.items()}
                if spent.is_finite() and all(v.is_finite() for v in days.values()):
                    return {"spent": spent, "as_of": c["as_of"], "days": days}
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError, InvalidOperation):
            pass
    key = resolve_admin_key(src)
    got = fetch_cost_report(key, start, end) if key else None
    if got is not None and not all(math.isfinite(float(v)) for v in [got["spent"]] + list(got["days"].values())):
        got = None   # e.g. "1E+400" cents: a finite Decimal, an infinite float
    if key is None:
        record = {"fetched_at": iso(now), "failed": True, "kind": "key-cmd"}
    elif got is None:
        record = {"fetched_at": iso(now), "failed": True}
    else:
        record = {"fetched_at": iso(now), "spent": str(got["spent"]), "as_of": got["as_of"],
                  "days": {k: str(v) for k, v in got["days"].items()}}
    cache.pop(ident, None)
    if len(cache) >= MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES:
        keep = sorted(cache, key=lambda k: cache[k].get("fetched_at", ""))[-(MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES - 1):]
        cache = {k: cache[k] for k in keep}
    cache[ident] = record
    try:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".api-credit-live.", suffix=".tmp", dir=os.path.dirname(path))
        try:
            with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
                f.write(json.dumps(cache) + "\n")
            os.replace(tmp, path)
        except BaseException:
            try:
                os.unlink(tmp)
            except OSError:
                pass
            raise
    except OSError:
        pass   # an unwritable cache only costs the next call a fetch
    return got


def with_provider(b, entries, grants_cfg, now):
    """Overlay the provider balance onto b when an admin key source is set and a
    live grant exists. The fetch window starts at the earliest grant in the
    overlap closure of the live grants, clamped to at most 366 days before today.
    Provider per-day sums in the window and ledger entries after the last bucket
    (plus pre-clamp ledger entries when clamped) are replayed soonest-expiry
    first. Each grant in the chain takes its lapse from the provider replay, and
    older grants take theirs from the ledger replay (also reported as
    ledger_lapsed_usd). estimate is False unless the window is clamped
    (provider_clamped), a grant starts or expires mid-UTC-day on a
    provider-bucket day (provider_subday), or any of the last
    SYG_CREDIT_SETTLE_DAYS closed days are unsettled (ledger > provider + EPS,
    provider_unsettled_days > 0). Any failure returns the labeled ledger
    fallback; b is untouched when no fetch is attempted."""
    src = admin_key_source()
    if src is None or grants_cfg is None:
        return b
    # live_of reads the sort and "lapsed" flags balance() set on grants_cfg[1] in
    # place; the window derives from that list, so a copying balance() breaks it.
    live = live_of(grants_cfg[1], now)
    if not live:
        return b
    s = min(g["granted"] for g in live)
    while True:
        older = [g["granted"] for g in grants_cfg[1]
                 if g["granted"] < s and (g["expires"] is None or g["expires"] > s)]
        if not older:
            break
        s = min(older)
    s_day, clamp, end = day_start(s), day_start(now) - timedelta(days=366), day_start(now)
    clamped = s_day < clamp
    start = max(s_day, clamp)
    if start >= end:
        return b   # no closed day since the earliest live grant: nothing to fetch
    start_day = start.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    b.update({"source": "ledger", "estimate": True, "provider_as_of": None,
              "provider_window_start": start_day, "ledger_bridge_days": None})
    try:
        got = provider_spend(src, start, end, now)
    except Exception:  # the balance must never fail on the live path
        got = None
    if got is None:
        return b
    as_of, s_key = got["as_of"], s_day.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    events = [e for e in entries if s_key <= e["day"] < start_day] if clamped else []
    day_rows, unsettled, _ = settled_days(got, entries, start, end)
    for d, _, amount in day_rows:
        when = min(d + timedelta(days=1) - timedelta(seconds=1), now)
        events.append({"last_ts": iso(when), "cost_usd": amount})
    bridged = [e for e in entries if e["day"] > as_of]
    subday = any(
        t is not None and start < t and t.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") <= as_of and t != day_start(t)
        for g in grants_cfg[1] for t in (g["granted"], g["expires"])
    )
    for i, g in enumerate(grants_cfg[1]):
        g["idx"] = i
    fresh_cfg = (grants_cfg[0], [dict(g, remaining=g["amount"], lapsed=False, lapsed_usd=0.0) for g in grants_cfg[1]])
    b.update(balance(events + bridged, fresh_cfg, now))
    by_idx = {pg["idx"]: pg for pg in fresh_cfg[1]}
    lapsed = sum((by_idx[lg["idx"]] if lg["granted"] >= s else lg).get("lapsed_usd", 0.0)
                 for lg in grants_cfg[1])
    ledger_lapsed = sum(lg.get("lapsed_usd", 0.0) for lg in grants_cfg[1] if lg["granted"] < s)
    b.update({"lapsed_usd": round(lapsed, 6), "ledger_lapsed_usd": round(ledger_lapsed, 6),
              "source": "provider", "estimate": clamped or subday or unsettled > 0,
              "provider_as_of": as_of, "provider_window_start": start_day,
              "provider_chain_start": s_key,
              "provider_clamped": clamped, "provider_subday": subday,
              "provider_unsettled_days": unsettled,
              "ledger_bridge_days": len({e["day"] for e in bridged})})
    return b


def with_month(b, entries, now):
    """Add month-to-date spend fields (month_start, month_spend_usd,
    month_as_of, month_source, month_estimate, month_bridge_days) to b for the
    current UTC month. Uses provider_spend for closed UTC days when an admin key
    source is set and the month has closed days (with the last
    SYG_CREDIT_SETTLE_DAYS closed days taking max(provider_day, ledger_day)),
    bridging later days from the ledger; falls back to the ledger on the 1st of
    the month, without a key, or on any failure."""
    end = day_start(now)
    start = end.replace(day=1)
    month_start, today = start.strftime("%Y-%m-%d"), end.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    ledger_spent = sum(e["cost_usd"] for e in entries if month_start <= e["day"] <= today)
    b.update({"month_start": month_start, "month_spend_usd": round(ledger_spent, 6),
              "month_as_of": None, "month_source": "ledger", "month_estimate": True,
              "month_bridge_days": 0})
    src = admin_key_source()
    if src is None or start >= end:
        return b
    if b.get("source") == "ledger" and b.get("provider_window_start") is not None:
        return b   # the balance fetch just failed: don't run the key command a second time
    try:
        got = provider_spend(src, start, end, now)
        if got is None:
            return b
        as_of = got["as_of"]
        if as_of < month_start:
            return b   # no provider bucket this month yet: the figure is all ledger
        _, unsettled, excess = settled_days(got, entries, start, end)
        bridged = [e for e in entries if month_start <= e["day"] <= today and e["day"] > as_of]
        spent = float(got["spent"]) + excess + sum(e["cost_usd"] for e in bridged)
        b.update({"month_spend_usd": round(spent, 6), "month_as_of": as_of,
                  "month_source": "provider", "month_estimate": unsettled > 0,
                  "month_bridge_days": len({e["day"] for e in bridged})})
    except Exception:  # the balance must never fail on the live path
        pass
    return b


def balance_text(b):
    """The one-line statusline text for a balance object: the bare figure when it
    is exact, followed by "est" when it is an estimate."""
    est = "" if b.get("estimate") is False else " est"
    if b["remaining_usd"] is None:
        s = "api $%s spent%s" % (money(b["spent_usd"]), est)
    elif b["remaining_usd"] > EPS:
        s = "api credit $%s%s" % (money(b["remaining_usd"]), est)
        if b["next_expiry"]:
            s += " (exp %s, %dd)" % (b["next_expiry"][5:10], b["days_left"])
    elif b["overage_usd"] > EPS:
        s = "api credit over $%s%s" % (money(b["overage_usd"]), est)
    else:
        s = "api credit $0.00" + est
    if "month_spend_usd" in b:
        m_est = "" if b.get("month_estimate") is False else " est"
        s += " · month $%s%s" % (money(b["month_spend_usd"]), m_est)
    return s


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- anchor

def anchor_path(ledger):
    return os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_ANCHOR", "") or ledger + ".anchor.json"


def read_anchor_doc(path):
    """The anchor file as a dict with an "anchors" list ({"anchors": []} when the
    file is missing). Raises ValueError when it exists but is unreadable."""
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            doc = json.load(f)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return {"anchors": []}
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        raise ValueError(str(exc))
    if not isinstance(doc, dict) or not isinstance(doc.get("anchors"), list):
        raise ValueError("no anchors list")
    return doc


def anchor_of(rec):
    """One anchor record -> {"amount", "at", "pre"}, or None when it is unusable."""
    if not isinstance(rec, dict):
        return None
    amount, pre = rec.get("amount"), rec.get("pre_anchor_day_usd")
    if not is_num(amount) or amount < 0 or not is_num(pre) or pre < 0 or not isinstance(rec.get("at"), str):
        return None
    try:
        at = parse_ts(rec["at"])
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return {"amount": float(amount), "at": at, "pre": float(pre)}


def governing_anchor(ledger, now, warn=False):
    """The usable anchor with the latest "at" no later than now (of equal ones, the
    last recorded), or None. An unreadable file is ignored (one stderr line when
    warn)."""
    path = anchor_path(ledger)
    try:
        doc = read_anchor_doc(path)
    except ValueError:
        if warn:
            print("api-credit: ignoring unreadable anchor file %s" % path, file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    best = None
    for rec in doc["anchors"]:
        a = anchor_of(rec)
        if a is not None and a["at"] <= now and (best is None or a["at"] >= best["at"]):
            best = a
    return best


def pool(amount, granted, expires):
    return {"amount": amount, "granted": granted, "expires": expires, "remaining": amount, "lapsed": False}


def anchor_pools(entries, grants, currency, anc):
    """Fresh pool dicts carrying the anchor's amount: the grants granted by the
    anchor are replayed to its instant (ledger days before its day plus the
    pre-anchor spend) for their remainders; the amount fills them latest-expiring
    first (no expiry = latest), each capped at its remainder, and the rest is one
    cash pool without expiry, kept even at 0."""
    t, day = anc["at"], anc["at"].strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    pre = [dict(g) for g in grants if g["granted"] <= t]
    if pre:
        replay = [e for e in entries if e["day"] < day] + [{"last_ts": iso(t), "cost_usd": anc["pre"]}]
        balance(replay, (currency, pre), t)   # sets each copy's remaining and lapsed
    left, pools = anc["amount"], []
    for g in sorted(pre, key=lambda g: g["expires"] or FAR, reverse=True):
        take = min(left, 0.0 if g["lapsed"] else max(g["remaining"], 0.0))
        if take > EPS:
            pools.append(pool(take, t, g["expires"]))
            left -= take
    pools.append(pool(left if left > EPS else 0.0, t, None))
    return pools


def anchor_day_event(day_entries, anc):
    """The anchor day's ledger spend after the anchor: that day's total minus the
    pre-anchor spend (clamped at 0), dated at the later of the anchor and the
    day's last request."""
    when, total = anc["at"], 0.0
    for e in day_entries:
        try:
            when = max(when, parse_ts(e["last_ts"]))
        except ValueError:
            continue   # no instant to date it at (balance() and pre_anchor_spend skip it too)
        total += e["cost_usd"]
    return {"last_ts": iso(when), "cost_usd": max(0.0, total - anc["pre"])}


def anchored_balance(entries, grants_cfg, now, anc):
    """The balance from an anchor: its pools plus the grants granted after it,
    minus the spend after it; provider figures for the closed days when the
    admin key answers."""
    currency, grants = grants_cfg if grants_cfg is not None else ("USD", [])
    t = anc["at"]
    day = t.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")

    def cfg():
        # balance() sorts and mutates its grant list: build a fresh one per call.
        return currency, anchor_pools(entries, grants, currency, anc) + [dict(g) for g in grants if g["granted"] > t]

    day_entries = [e for e in entries if e["day"] == day]
    events = [e for e in entries if e["day"] > day] + [anchor_day_event(day_entries, anc)]
    b = balance(events, cfg(), now)
    b.update({"anchor_at": iso(t), "anchor_usd": round(anc["amount"], 6)})

    src = admin_key_source()
    if src is None:
        return b
    start, end = day_start(t), day_start(now)
    if start >= end:
        return b   # no closed day since the anchor's day: nothing to fetch
    b.update({"source": "ledger", "estimate": True, "provider_as_of": None,
              "provider_window_start": day, "ledger_bridge_days": None})
    try:
        got = provider_spend(src, start, end, now)
    except Exception:  # the balance must never fail on the live path
        got = None
    if got is None:
        return b
    as_of, events = got["as_of"], []
    day_rows, unsettled, _ = settled_days(got, entries, start, end)
    for d, dk, amount in day_rows:
        when = min(d + timedelta(days=1) - timedelta(seconds=1), now)
        if dk == day:
            amount, when = max(0.0, amount - anc["pre"]), max(t, when)
        events.append({"last_ts": iso(when), "cost_usd": amount})
    bridged = [e for e in entries if e["day"] > as_of and e["day"] > day]
    used = {e["day"] for e in bridged}
    if day > as_of:
        events.append(anchor_day_event(day_entries, anc))
        used.update(e["day"] for e in day_entries)
    b.update(balance(events + bridged, cfg(), now))
    b.update({"source": "provider", "estimate": unsettled > 0, "provider_as_of": as_of,
              "provider_window_start": day, "provider_unsettled_days": unsettled,
              "ledger_bridge_days": len(used)})
    return b


class CalibrateError(Exception):
    pass


def usage_exit(msg):
    print("api-credit: %s" % msg, file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)


def parse_instant(raw):
    """A full ISO-8601 timestamp with an offset or Z -> UTC datetime; None for a
    date-only value, a missing offset or garbage."""
    s = raw.strip()
    t = s[:-1] + "+00:00" if s[-1:] in ("Z", "z") else s
    try:
        dt = datetime.fromisoformat(t)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if dt.tzinfo is None or len(s) <= 10:
        return None
    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc)


def pre_anchor_spend(entries, t):
    """The spend on t's UTC day before t (see Anchor). Every session in the ledger
    (any day) whose transcript (its latest entry's transcript_path) was modified
    on or after 00:00 UTC of that day is read once, so an unhooked turn counts
    even for a session whose entries are all on earlier days; older transcripts
    cannot hold that day's requests and are skipped unread. The day's entries of
    the other sessions take the whole/zero rule. Raises CalibrateError for such an
    entry whose requests straddle t."""
    day, prices, total = t.strftime("%Y-%m-%d"), None, 0.0
    since = day_start(t).timestamp()
    # The hook's rule, built once: a request another session's entry holds is not
    # this session's; one no entry holds yet (an unhooked turn) is.
    owners, latest = {}, {}
    for e in entries:
        sid = e["session_id"]
        if isinstance(e.get("request_ids"), list):
            for x in e["request_ids"]:
                if isinstance(x, str):
                    owners.setdefault(x, set()).add(sid)
        key = (e["day"], e["last_ts"])
        if sid not in latest or key > latest[sid][0]:
            latest[sid] = (key, e.get("transcript_path"))
    read = set()
    for sid, (_, tpath) in latest.items():
        if not isinstance(tpath, str) or not tpath:
            continue
        try:
            st = os.stat(tpath)
        except OSError:
            continue   # gone: the session's entries of the day take the whole/zero rule
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode) or st.st_mtime < since:
            continue   # older than the day: no request of it inside
        if prices is None:
            prices = load_prices()
        read.add(sid)
        requests, _ = extract(transcript_sources(sid, tpath))
        for r in requests:
            if r["request_id"] is not None and any(o != sid for o in owners.get(r["request_id"], ())):
                continue
            if r["ts"].strftime("%Y-%m-%d") != day or r["ts"] >= t:
                continue
            rates = rates_for(prices, r["model"])
            if rates is not None:   # unpriced: no cost, as the hook records it
                total += request_cost(r, rates)
    for e in entries:
        sid = e["session_id"]
        if e["day"] != day or sid in read:
            continue
        try:
            last = parse_ts(e["last_ts"])
            first = parse_ts(e["first_ts"]) if isinstance(e.get("first_ts"), str) else last
        except ValueError:
            continue   # no instant to compare (balance() skips it too)
        if last < t:
            total += e["cost_usd"]
        elif first < t:
            raise CalibrateError("cannot split session %s's %s spend at %s: its transcript is gone; "
                                 "choose --at outside %s..%s" % (sid, day, iso(t), iso(first), iso(last)))
    return total


def calibrate(amount_raw, at_raw):
    """Append an anchor record (see Anchor) and print it with the new balance."""
    ledger = need_ledger()
    try:
        amount = float(amount_raw)
    except ValueError:
        amount = float("nan")
    if not math.isfinite(amount) or amount < 0:
        usage_exit("calibrate AMOUNT must be a finite number >= 0, got %r" % amount_raw)
    amount += 0.0   # -0 -> +0.0, so it never stores or prints as -0
    now = utcnow()
    t = now if at_raw is None else parse_instant(at_raw)
    if t is None:
        usage_exit("--at needs a full ISO-8601 timestamp with an offset or Z (an anchor is a "
                   "precise instant), got %r" % at_raw)
    t = t.replace(microsecond=0)   # the stored instant has whole seconds; compute with that one
    if t > now:
        usage_exit("--at %s is later than now (%s)" % (iso(t), iso(now)))
    path = anchor_path(ledger)
    for p in (ledger, path):
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(p)), exist_ok=True)
    with open(ledger + ".lock", "a") as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        try:
            doc = read_anchor_doc(path)
        except ValueError:
            raise CalibrateError("refusing to overwrite unreadable anchor file %s" % path)
        entries, _ = read_ledger(ledger)
        pre = pre_anchor_spend(entries, t)
        doc["anchors"].append({"amount": amount, "at": iso(t), "pre_anchor_day_usd": round(pre, 6),
                               "recorded": iso(now)})
        write_atomic(path, [json.dumps(doc, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)])
    print("anchored $%s at %s (same-day spend before it $%s)" % (money(amount), iso(t), money(pre)))
    try:
        print(balance_text(current_balance()))
    except Exception as exc:  # the anchor is written: report, never fail the command
        print("api-credit: balance failed: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- daily

def daily(entries):
    days = {}
    for e in entries:
        row = days.setdefault(e["day"], {"day": e["day"], "sids": set(), "cost_usd": 0.0, "models": set()})
        row["sids"].add(e["session_id"])
        row["cost_usd"] += e["cost_usd"]
        row["models"].update(e.get("models") or [])
    rows = [{"day": r["day"], "sessions": len(r["sids"]), "cost_usd": round(r["cost_usd"], 6),
             "models": sorted(r["models"])} for _, r in sorted(days.items())]
    total = {"sessions": len({e["session_id"] for e in entries}),
             "cost_usd": round(sum(e["cost_usd"] for e in entries), 6)}
    return rows, total


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- commands

def read_payload():
    try:
        return json.loads(sys.stdin.read())
    except ValueError:
        return None


def safe_hook(payload):
    try:
        hook(payload)
    except Exception as exc:  # a hook must never block the session
        print("api-credit: hook failed: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)


def need_ledger():
    path = os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER", "")
    if not path:
        print("api-credit: SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER is not set", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    return path


def current_balance(warn=False, month=False):
    """The balance for the read-only commands (balance, statusline): the ledger
    estimate, replaced by the provider figures when the live path answers; from
    the governing anchor when there is one (warn: say so on stderr when the
    anchor file is unreadable). With month, adds month-to-date spend."""
    ledger = need_ledger()
    entries, _ = read_ledger(ledger)
    grants_cfg, now = load_grants(), utcnow()
    anc = governing_anchor(ledger, now, warn)
    if anc is not None:
        b = anchored_balance(entries, grants_cfg, now, anc)
    else:
        b = with_provider(balance(entries, grants_cfg, now), entries, grants_cfg, now)
    return with_month(b, entries, now) if month else b


def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="api-credit", description="API spend ledger and credit estimate")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    sub.add_parser("hook")
    sp = sub.add_parser("statusline")
    sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    bp = sub.add_parser("balance")
    bp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    bp.add_argument("--month", action="store_true")
    dp = sub.add_parser("daily")
    dp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    cp = sub.add_parser("calibrate")
    cp.add_argument("amount")
    cp.add_argument("--at")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)

    if args.cmd == "hook":
        if os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER") and route_matches():
            safe_hook(read_payload())
        return 0
    if args.cmd == "statusline":
        # Read-only: recording is the hook's job.
        if not os.environ.get("SYG_CREDIT_LEDGER"):
            return 0
        try:
            b = current_balance()
        except Exception as exc:
            print("api-credit: balance failed: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
            return 0
        print(json.dumps(b, sort_keys=True) if args.json else balance_text(b))
        return 0
    if args.cmd == "balance":
        b = current_balance(warn=True, month=args.month)
        if args.json:
            print(json.dumps(b, sort_keys=True))
        else:
            print(balance_text(b))
            if b.get("source") == "provider":
                parts = ["today"]
                if "anchor_at" in b:   # the anchored replay's lapses come from the ledger
                    parts.append("lapsed")
                if b.get("ledger_lapsed_usd", 0) > 0:
                    parts.append("lapses before %s" % (b.get("provider_chain_start") or b.get("provider_window_start")))
                if b.get("provider_clamped"):
                    parts.append("spend before %s" % b.get("provider_window_start"))
                ledger_part = (parts[0] + " from the ledger" if len(parts) == 1 else
                               "%s and %s, from the ledger" % (", ".join(parts[:-1]), parts[-1]))
                basis = "provider through %s; %s" % (b["provider_as_of"], ledger_part)
                if b.get("provider_subday"):
                    basis += "; grant times mid-day"
            else:
                basis = "estimate"
            if "anchor_at" in b:
                basis += "; anchored $%s at %s" % (money(b["anchor_usd"]), b["anchor_at"])
            print("spent $%s, lapsed $%s, overage $%s (%s)"
                  % (money(b["spent_usd"]), money(b["lapsed_usd"]), money(b["overage_usd"]), basis))
        return 0
    if args.cmd == "calibrate":
        try:
            calibrate(args.amount, args.at)
        except CalibrateError as exc:
            print("api-credit: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        except Exception as exc:  # e.g. a failing price table: nothing was written
            print("api-credit: calibrate failed: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        return 0
    if args.cmd == "daily":
        entries, _ = read_ledger(need_ledger())
        rows, total = daily(entries)
        if args.json:
            print(json.dumps({"days": rows, "total": total}, sort_keys=True))
        else:
            for r in rows:
                print("%s  $%s  %d sessions  %s" % (r["day"], money(r["cost_usd"]), r["sessions"], ",".join(r["models"])))
            print("total       $%s  %d sessions" % (money(total["cost_usd"]), total["sessions"]))
        return 0
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
